From 34d911de175ba574de897b6427f006754bda2625 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: beau4201 <beau.ten.berge@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:56:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] oblivios: show inline autofill suggestions as chips in the
 suggestion strip

The keyboard now declares inline suggestion support and shows the chips of the autofill service in a new row of the suggestion strip, which has priority over the paste actions and the word suggestions. The system draws the chip in another process from the content of the service and a style that this keyboard sends in its request; the keyboard receives a surface only, sets an exact size for every chip (260 dp alone, 158 dp when several share the strip) so that the width tells nothing about the text, and never reads, logs or captures a suggestion. A typed or deleted character ends the offer for the field until the next request. The request is built without the input view, because the platform may ask before the view exists. The strip is hidden on password fields today; it is now shown while chips are there, so that the login of a password field can be offered. No supportsInlineSuggestionsWithTouchExploration: with TalkBack on, the system list is used. ADR-191.
